          "date": "2026-11-12 21:55:05.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-10868 build: strip debug info from deb kernel modules",
        "message": "LU-10868 build: strip debug info from deb kernel modules\n\nThe Debian packages that ship kernel modules, the\nlustre-{client,server}-modules packages and lustre-tests, carry every\n.ko with its full DWARF and have no -dbgsym package for them.  The\nmodules are built with -g and dh_strip never touches them: it only\nhandles ET_EXEC, ET_DYN and static libraries, while a kernel module\nis ET_REL.  binary-modules, which module-assistant runs, has no other\nstrip step.  The RPM build makes modules visible to find-debuginfo.sh\nexplicitly, so it does not have this problem.\n\nAdd strip_ko, which binary-modules runs and which lustre-tests runs\nafter dh_strip.  It moves the debug info of each module into a\nbuild-id keyed -dbgsym package, laid out as dh_strip does so that\ndh_gencontrol and dh_builddeb build it, then strips the module with\n--strip-debug.  dh_strip has already started the -dbgsym package of\nlustre-tests for its binaries, so the build-ids of its modules are\nappended to the same one-line list.  Keep .symtab, which module\nloading needs, and the .BTF and .BTF.base sections that pahole adds.\nHonor nostrip, noautodbgsym and noddebs in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS as\ndh_strip does, and let STRIP, OBJCOPY and READELF be overridden.\nFail the build if a module has no build-id.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ralph Goff <ralph.goff@netapp.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I0ae9ba8b8e15dc1e4e02742e0e57e4008cbd5955\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
